int4 per-token-head KV cache with the DFlash2 drafter: three boot blockers.

`--attention-backend TRITON_ATTN --kv-cache-dtype int4_per_token_head` +
`SPEC=dflash2` dies at engine start on stock-plus-this-stack. Fixed, it serves
256k max-model-len on one 24 GB card with a 314,915-token pool (1.23x
concurrency at 256k) — more than CTX=huge/KVarN's 268k, on stock vLLM
machinery — at a decode cost from the Triton backend and the per-step int4
unpack (~86 tok/s e2e on a short-prose probe vs ~104 for the shipped
FLASH_ATTN bf16 config, same probe). `single-user/alternative.sh` is the
launcher for this profile.

The three mechanisms, in boot order:

1. v1/worker/gpu/attn_utils.py — the padded-page view. With
   0012-hybrid-sw-block-promote.patch in place, the drafter's sliding-window layer
   is promoted and every other layer's page is *padded* up to the promoted
   maximum, so the raw KV tensor holds more bytes per block than the logical
   shape needs. The flat `.view(dtype).view(shape)` cannot express that:

     RuntimeError: shape '[380, 848, 8, 136]' is invalid for input of size
     680570880

   (680,570,880 allocated, 350,597,120 needed — the padding lives at the tail
   of every block, not the tail of the tensor). Reproduced on this card at
   engine init with the alternative.sh config. The fix views (num_blocks,
   raw_per_block), narrows each block to the bytes the logical shape wants,
   and reshapes. Gated on per-token-head quant modes plus exact divisibility;
   bf16/int8/fp8 caches take the old single-view path byte-identically.

2. v1/attention/ops/triton_unified_attention.py — the INT4_PER_TOKEN_HEAD
   branch asserted causal-only attention. The DFlash2 drafter's
   sliding-window layers run the 8-row draft block as per-seq-causal query
   attention, so SPEC=dflash2 tripped the assert before the first token.
   Dropped; use_causal / per_seq_causal_ptr are forwarded instead.

3. v1/attention/ops/int4_per_token_head.py — the packed kernel now takes
   USE_CAUSAL / USE_PER_SEQ_CAUSAL constexprs and the per-seq pointer,
   plumbed through _attn_packed and both launchers. Defaults reproduce the
   old causal-only behavior exactly.

Verified here (RTX 3090, 250 W): unpatched boot reproduces the RuntimeError
above; patched boot serves — coherent prose, tool-calling round trip with
well-formed arguments (composes with 0014-xgrammar-spec-terminated.patch), lookup
lane active on verbatim reproduction. Shipped-config inertness: production
FLASH_ATTN + bf16 boot pool is byte-identical (57,669 tokens) and none of the
modified branches are reachable under it. Quality at depth (needle, GSM8K)
has not been measured on int4 KV — treat the profile as experimental.

Provenance: PR #42 by Walid Lachhab (@lachhabw), rebased onto this patch
stack. Their submission was cut against stock 0.27.1 and therefore re-shipped
the kv_cache_utils.py block-promotion/grouping functions this repo already
carries in 0012-hybrid-sw-block-promote.patch (dropped here), plus a mamba
GCD-hash change whose branch is unreachable under the launchers'
`--mamba-cache-mode align` (dropped; details in the PR thread).

